-- title:
--   Local points hitting the j-finite chart factor through it
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, $K$ a field equipped with an $A$-algebra structure, and $j \in K$ with $j \neq 0$. Write $R =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of those elements of $K$ that are integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, i.e. the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, and let [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) be the canonical morphism from the affine chart $\operatorname{Spec} R$ into the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229), the latter being the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin` and `fInf` of affine schemes induced by the inclusions of the chart algebras into the overlap algebra. Let $O$ be a commutative local ring and let $\xi : \operatorname{Spec} O \to$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) be a morphism of schemes whose underlying continuous map sends the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$ into the image of the underlying map of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231). The conclusion is that there exists a ring homomorphism $\psi : R \to O$ such that $\xi$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(\psi)$ followed by [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231).
--
--   This is the standard fact that a morphism from the spectrum of a local ring into a scheme factors through any open subscheme containing the image of the closed point, specialised to the $j$-finite affine chart of the two-chart model and combined with the description of morphisms into affine schemes as spectra of ring homomorphisms. It is used in the reduction statements for $X_1(Mp)$, where $O$ is the valuation ring of a place and the reduction of an $O$-valued point of the model is known to lie in the $j$-finite chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_TwoChart_exists_eq_spec_map_comp_iotaFin_of_apply_closedPoint_mem_range.lean

